<!--
    C function prototypes from SDK headers (`option objcsdk <dir>|off`, the C
    half of the option).

    Issue: `objcsdk` read only Objective-C declarations, so the C functions the
    same headers declare had no prototype. A call whose arguments were set up
    before an earlier call lost them (`v2 = CFStringGetLength();`), a tail call
    printed bare (`dispatch_async_f(); // tail-call`), a struct filled through
    a pointer was loose stack slots, and an enum constant was a number.

    Stage / sub-stage: P1 external-refinement.
    `analyzers/protos/kuna_sdkprotos.rs` reads the declarations of the names the
    image imports from the same directory: attribute macros skipped, the `#if`
    branches the target rules out dropped, types resolved through typedefs,
    records, the enum macros and the object macros. A by-value struct is spread
    over registers only where its members travel as separate arguments would.

    P0 assertion: `option objcsdk <directory>|off` (env-bridged, load-time: set
    before the `load file` it applies to and cleared at the end).

    The fixture is `macho_sdk_c.c`, built against the hand-written stand-in
    headers in `tests/fixtures/sdk_c/` (no SDK text), every callee an import.

    Pass 1 (no headers) reproduces the BUG. Pass 2 (`objcsdk` pointed at the
    header directory) is the FIX. `GadgetAmbiguous` (declared two ways) and
    `GadgetOpaque` (a by-value type no header defines) keep no prototype in
    both passes.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c0035fd6
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
